{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 21: a distributor's ordering policy, with a running cost of holding stock and of backorders, ready for optimisation. }
Base Demand=
	100
	~	units/week
	~	Customer demand before the change.
	|
Step Height=
	20
	~	units/week
	~	Permanent rise in demand at week 10.
	|
Season Amplitude=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Seasonal swing as a fraction of base demand (52-week cycle).
	|
Noise Level=
	15
	~	units/week
	~	Standard deviation of week-to-week noise in demand.
	|
Noise Correlation Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	How long a run of high or low demand typically lasts.
	|
White Noise=
	Noise Level * SQRT(2 * Noise Correlation Time / TIME STEP) * RANDOM NORMAL(-6, 6, 0, 1, Noise Seed)
	~	units/week
	~	Independent draws each time step, scaled so the smoothed noise has standard deviation Noise Level.
	|
Demand Noise= INTEG(
	(White Noise - Demand Noise) / Noise Correlation Time,
	0)
	~	units/week
	~	Pink (autocorrelated) noise in demand.
	|
Noise Seed=
	1
	~	dmnl
	~	Seed of the random demand noise (one seed, one demand history).
	|
Demand=
	MAX(0, Base Demand * (1 + Season Amplitude * SIN(2 * 3.14159 * Time / Season Period)) + STEP(Step Height, 10) + Demand Noise)
	~	units/week
	~	Orders from customers.
	|
Season Period=
	52
	~	week
	~		|
Forecast Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	Time to adjust the demand forecast.
	|
Expected Demand=
	SMOOTH(Demand, Forecast Time)
	~	units/week
	~	Smoothed demand used for ordering.
	|
Safety Weeks=
	2
	~	week
	~	Weeks of expected demand held as safety stock (lever).
	|
Desired Inventory=
	Safety Weeks * Expected Demand
	~	units
	~		|
Initial Inventory=
	Safety Weeks * Base Demand
	~	units
	~	Start in balance with the safety stock.
	|
Net Inventory= INTEG(
	Arrivals - Demand,
	Initial Inventory)
	~	units
	~	Stock on hand minus backorders (negative means customers are waiting).
	|
Supply Delay=
	4
	~	week
	~	Average time from order to arrival.
	|
Initial Supply Line=
	Supply Delay * Base Demand
	~	units
	~	Start in balance.
	|
Supply Line= INTEG(
	Orders - Arrivals,
	Initial Supply Line)
	~	units
	~	Ordered but not yet received.
	|
Arrivals=
	Supply Line / Supply Delay
	~	units/week
	~		|
Adjustment Time=
	2
	~	week
	~	Time over which inventory and supply line gaps are closed (lever).
	|
Supply Line Weight=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Fraction of the supply line gap the ordering rule corrects (lever).
	|
Desired Supply Line=
	Supply Delay * Expected Demand
	~	units
	~		|
Rule Orders=
	MAX(0, Expected Demand + (Desired Inventory - Net Inventory) / Adjustment Time + Supply Line Weight * (Desired Supply Line - Supply Line) / Adjustment Time)
	~	units/week
	~	The stock management rule.
	|
Plan Orders=
	100
	~	units/week
	~	Orders set by an outside plan (model predictive control writes this equation).
	|
Plan Mode=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	1: orders follow Plan Orders; 0: the rule.
	|
Supplier Capacity=
	1000
	~	units/week
	~	Most the supplier can accept in a week (1000: no limit).
	|
Orders=
	MIN(Supplier Capacity, IF THEN ELSE(Plan Mode > 0.5, Plan Orders, Rule Orders))
	~	units/week
	~		|
Holding Cost=
	0.2
	~	dollar/unit/week
	~	Cost of keeping one unit in stock for a week.
	|
Backorder Cost=
	2
	~	dollar/unit/week
	~	Cost of making one customer unit wait a week.
	|
Holding Cost Rate=
	Holding Cost * MAX(Net Inventory, 0)
	~	dollar/week
	~		|
Backorder Cost Rate=
	Backorder Cost * MAX(-Net Inventory, 0)
	~	dollar/week
	~		|
Total Holding Cost= INTEG(
	Holding Cost Rate,
	0)
	~	dollar
	~		|
Total Backorder Cost= INTEG(
	Backorder Cost Rate,
	0)
	~	dollar
	~		|
Order Change Cost=
	5
	~	dollar/unit
	~	Cost of departing from the expected demand rate, per unit of departure each week, scaled by base demand.
	|
Order Variation Cost Rate=
	Order Change Cost * (Orders - Expected Demand) * (Orders - Expected Demand) / Base Demand
	~	dollar/week
	~	Quadratic cost of erratic orders (overtime, expediting and upstream amplification).
	|
Total Order Variation Cost= INTEG(
	Order Variation Cost Rate,
	0)
	~	dollar
	~		|
Backorder Unit Weeks= INTEG(
	MAX(-Net Inventory, 0),
	0)
	~	unit*week
	~	Customer units kept waiting, summed over the weeks they waited (a service measure).
	|
Operating Cost=
	Total Holding Cost + Total Order Variation Cost
	~	dollar
	~	Cost of stock and of erratic ordering, without the cost of backorders.
	|
Total Cost=
	Total Holding Cost + Total Backorder Cost + Total Order Variation Cost
	~	dollar
	~	The objective.
	|
FINAL TIME = 104 ~ week ~ |
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
